---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';
import { breadcrumbSchema, graph, organizationSchema } from '../lib/seo';

const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', href: '/' },
  { name: 'Terms of use', href: '/terms/' },
];

const schema = graph([
  organizationSchema(),
  breadcrumbSchema(breadcrumbs),
  {
    '@type': 'WebPage',
    name: 'Terms of use',
    url: `${SITE.url}/terms/`,
    isPartOf: { '@id': `${SITE.url}/#website` },
  },
]);
---

<PageLayout
  title="Terms of Use"
  description="The terms governing your use of HostScope, including the limits of our accuracy guarantees and the independence of our editorial content."
  eyebrow="Legal"
  canonical={`${SITE.url}/terms/`}
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
  schema={schema}
  updated={new Date('2026-09-10')}
>
  <p class="lead text-[1.125rem] text-ink-700">
    By using HostScope you agree to these terms. They are short and, we hope, readable.
  </p>

  <h2 id="who-we-are">Who we are</h2>

  <p>
    HostScope is published by {SITE.publisher.legalName}. We are an independent publication. We are
    not affiliated with, endorsed by, or operated by Hostinger International Ltd or any other hosting
    provider mentioned on this site.
  </p>

  <h2 id="accuracy">Accuracy of information</h2>

  <p>
    We work hard to keep prices, specifications and limits accurate, and we record the date each set
    of figures was verified. The current verification date is{' '}
    <strong>{SITE.pricingVerified}</strong>.
  </p>

  <p>
    That said, hosting pricing changes frequently and without notice. We cannot guarantee that every
    figure on this site matches the price you will be quoted at checkout. <strong>The merchant's
    checkout page is always the authoritative source.</strong> Nothing on this site is an offer, and
    we are not a party to any transaction you enter into with a hosting provider.
  </p>

  <h2 id="no-advice">No professional advice</h2>

  <p>
    Our articles are editorial opinion and general information. They are not legal, financial or
    professional advice for your specific circumstances. Decisions about hosting, spending and
    infrastructure are yours to make and yours to own.
  </p>

  <h2 id="affiliate">Affiliate relationships</h2>

  <p>
    This site contains affiliate links. If you buy hosting through one, we may receive a commission at
    no additional cost to you. Full details are on the{' '}
    <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure page</a>, and our editorial standards are
    set out in the <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="third-party">Third-party services</h2>

  <p>
    We link to third-party websites, including hosting providers and review platforms. We do not
    control those sites and are not responsible for their content, terms, pricing, availability or
    practices. Following an outbound link means you accept that site's terms.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ip">Intellectual property</h2>

  <p>
    The text, design and original graphics on this site are owned by {SITE.publisher.legalName} and
    protected by copyright. You may quote short excerpts with clear attribution and a link. You may
    not republish articles in full, reproduce them for commercial purposes, or use them to train
    machine learning models without written permission.
  </p>

  <p>
    "Hostinger" and other product names mentioned are trademarks of their respective owners. Their use
    here is descriptive and does not imply endorsement or affiliation.
  </p>

  <h2 id="liability">Limitation of liability</h2>

  <p>
    This site is provided "as is" and "as available". To the maximum extent permitted by law, we
    exclude all warranties, express or implied, and we are not liable for any loss or damage arising
    from your use of this site or from any decision you make based on its content — including loss of
    data, loss of profit, or costs incurred with a hosting provider.
  </p>

  <h2 id="acceptable-use">Acceptable use</h2>

  <p>
    You agree not to scrape this site at a rate that degrades service for other readers, attempt to
    compromise its security, or reproduce its content in bulk without permission.
  </p>

  <h2 id="changes">Changes to these terms</h2>

  <p>
    We may update these terms. The "last updated" date at the top of the page will change when we do,
    and continued use of the site after a change constitutes acceptance.
  </p>

  <h2 id="governing-law">Governing law</h2>

  <p>
    These terms are governed by the laws of the State of California, United States, without regard to
    conflict-of-law principles.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>

  <p>
    Questions about these terms: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.publisher.email}`}>{SITE.publisher.email}</a>
  </p>
</PageLayout>
